        'Imagine a toy allocator that reserves space for 64 tokens whenever a request arrives. A request that stops after 17 tokens uses only 17 of those slots, leaving 47 reserved but unused. Across many variable-length requests, this waste reduces concurrency even though useful KV data would fit. Choosing a smaller contiguous reservation creates a different problem when a request grows beyond it. The allocator needs growth without guessing every answer’s final length in advance.',
